Yabushita</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanaly</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Shibutani</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yokoyama</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Increased DNA damage in ALDH2-deficient alcoholics</article-title><source>Chem Res Toxicol</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>1374</fpage><lpage>1378</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17040107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000050-b018"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fukao</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yokoyama</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Genotoxic effects of alcohol in human peripheral lymphocytes modulated by ADH1B and ALDH2 gene polymorphisms</article-title><source>Mutat Res</source><volume>615</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>142</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17207821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000050-b019"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Baan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Straif</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Grosse</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Secretan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>El Ghissassi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Carcinogenicity of alcoholic beverages</article-title><source>Lancet Oncol</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>292</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17431955</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000050-b020"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Lachenmeier</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sohnius</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The role of acetaldehyde outside ethanol metabolism in the carcinogenicity of alcoholic beverages: Evidence from a large chemical survey</article-title><source>Food Chem Toxicol</source><volume>46</volume><fpage>2903</fpage><lpage>2911</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18577414</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000050-b021"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Homann</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tillonen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Meurman</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rintamaki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindqvist</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Increased salivary acetaldehyde levels in heavy drinkers and smokers: A microbiological approach to oral cavity cancer</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>663</fpage><lpage>668</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10753201</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-1000050-b022"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Vakevainen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tillonen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Agarwal</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Srivastava</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Salaspuro</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>High salivary acetaldehyde after a moderate dose of alcohol in ALDH2-deficient subjects: Strong evidence for the local carcinogenic action of acetaldehyde</article-title><source>Alcohol Clin Exp Res</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>873</fpage><lpage>877</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10888077</pu